NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI provides framework hooks for every generation type: image, audio, speech, transcription, summarization, and video. Each hook connects to a server endpoint and manages loading, error, and result state for you."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Surviving reloads and dropped connections:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" every generation hook takes the\nsame "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" option "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" does, so a long run's status and result\ncome back after a page reload or a dropped connection. It restores by\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", which for a generation names the slot successive runs fill\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"product-7-hero"},{"type":"text","value":") rather than a conversation. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/id-map","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Id map"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Setup is in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/generation-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation hooks share a consistent API across all media types:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result Type"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateImage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerateInput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerationResult"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateAudio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AudioGenerateInput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AudioGenerationResult"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateSpeech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SpeechGenerateInput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TTSResult"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTranscription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TranscriptionGenerateInput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TranscriptionResult"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSummarize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SummarizeGenerateInput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SummarizationResult"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateVideo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoGenerateInput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoGenerateResult"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGeneration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TInput"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TResult"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every hook returns the same core shape: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":" (the id of the job in flight, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"). You provide either a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"},{"type":"text","value":" (streaming transport) or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetcher"},{"type":"text","value":" (direct async call)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before using hooks on the client, you need a server endpoint that runs the generation and returns the result as SSE. Here's a minimal image generation endpoint:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/generate/image.ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(req: Request) {\n  const { prompt, size, numberOfImages } = await req.json()\n\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: openaiImage('dall-e-3'),\n    prompt,\n    size,\n    numberOfImages,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same pattern applies to image, speech, transcription, summarize, and video. Live and world generation mint a session token. Connect in the browser. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./live-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"./world-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"World Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usegenerateimage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useGenerateImage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trigger image generation and render the results."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a React + Start walkthrough with OpenRouter, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/generate-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate Image"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useState } from 'react'\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, reset } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(e) => setPrompt(e.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Describe an image...\"\n      />\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt })}\n        disabled={isLoading || !prompt.trim()}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img\n          key={i}\n          src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`}\n          alt={img.revisedPrompt || 'Generated image'}\n        />\n      ))}\n\n      {result && <button onClick={reset}>Clear</button>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ImageGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text description of the desired image (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"numberOfImages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Number of images to generate"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image size in WIDTHxHEIGHT format (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"1024x1024\""},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model-specific options"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usegenerateaudio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useGenerateAudio"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate music or sound effects from a text prompt."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you use a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetcher"},{"type":"text","value":", spread "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.headers"},{"type":"text","value":" onto the POST. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok"},{"type":"text","value":" so those headers include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" keys."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateAudio } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-client/byok'\n\nconst byok = defineByok({ storage: defaultByokStorage() })\n\nfunction AudioGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateAudio({\n    byok,\n    byokProvider: () => 'fal',\n    fetcher: async (input, options) => {\n      return fetch('/api/generate/audio', {\n        method: 'POST',\n        headers: {\n          'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n          ...options?.headers,\n        },\n        body: JSON.stringify(input),\n        signal: options?.signal,\n      })\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: 'An upbeat electronic track' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate'}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result?.audio.url && <audio src={result.audio.url} controls />}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server: read the header (or env), then run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateAudio"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateAudio, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falAudio } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\nimport { falByok } from '@tanstack/ai-fal/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, falByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(falByok)\n\n  const body: unknown = await request.json()\n  if (typeof body !== 'object' || body === null || !('prompt' in body)) {\n    return new Response('Bad request', { status: 400 })\n  }\n  const prompt = body.prompt\n  if (typeof prompt !== 'string') {\n    return new Response('Bad request', { status: 400 })\n  }\n\n  const stream = generateAudio({\n    adapter: falAudio('fal-ai/minimax-music/v2.6', { apiKey }),\n    prompt,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AudioGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text description of the desired audio (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Desired duration in seconds"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model-specific options"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineByok"},{"type":"text","value":" and a save UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usegeneratespeech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useGenerateSpeech"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Convert text to speech and play it back."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useRef } from 'react'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const audioRef = useRef<HTMLAudioElement>(null)\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!', voice: 'alloy' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Speech'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <audio\n          ref={audioRef}\n          src={`data:audio/${result.format};base64,${result.audio}`}\n          controls\n          autoPlay\n        />\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SpeechGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The text to convert to speech (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The voice to use (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"alloy\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"echo\""},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'mp3' | 'opus' | 'aac' | 'flac' | 'wav' | 'pcm'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Output audio format"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"speed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio speed (0.25 to 4.0)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model-specific options"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TTSResult"},{"type":"text","value":" contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio"},{"type":"text","value":" (base64-encoded), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", and optionally "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contentType"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usetranscription","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useTranscription"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcribe audio files to text."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useTranscription, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Transcriber() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useTranscription({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/transcribe'),\n  })\n\n  const handleFile = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n    const file = e.target.files?.[0]\n    if (file) {\n      const reader = new FileReader()\n      reader.onload = () => {\n        generate({ audio: reader.result as string, language: 'en' })\n      }\n      reader.readAsDataURL(file)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input type=\"file\" accept=\"audio/*\" onChange={handleFile} />\n\n      {isLoading && <p>Transcribing...</p>}\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <div>\n          <h3>Transcription</h3>\n          <p>{result.text}</p>\n          {result.language && <p>Language: {result.language}</p>}\n          {result.duration && <p>Duration: {result.duration}s</p>}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TranscriptionGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | File | Blob | ArrayBuffer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio data -- base64 string, File, Blob, or ArrayBuffer (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"language"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language in ISO-639-1 format (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"en\""},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional prompt to guide the transcription"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"responseFormat"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'json' | 'text' | 'srt' | 'verbose_json' | 'vtt'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common output format"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model-specific options"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usesummarize","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useSummarize"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarize long text with configurable output styles."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useSummarize, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useState } from 'react'\n\nfunction Summarizer() {\n  const [text, setText] = useState('')\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useSummarize({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/summarize'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <textarea\n        value={text}\n        onChange={(e) => setText(e.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Paste text to summarize...\"\n        rows={8}\n      />\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text, style: 'bullet-points', maxLength: 200 })}\n        disabled={isLoading || !text.trim()}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Summarizing...' : 'Summarize'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <div>\n          <h3>Summary</h3>\n          <p>{result.summary}</p>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SummarizeGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The text to summarize (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxLength"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maximum length of the summary"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'bullet-points' | 'paragraph' | 'concise'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summary style"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focus"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<string>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Topics to focus on"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model-specific options"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usegeneratevideo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useGenerateVideo"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video generation is asynchronous -- a job is created on the server, then polled for status until completion. The hook manages the full lifecycle and exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"jobId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"videoStatus"},{"type":"text","value":" so you can show progress."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateVideo, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction VideoGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, jobId, videoStatus, isLoading, error } =\n    useGenerateVideo({\n      connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/video'),\n      onStatusUpdate: (status) => {\n        console.log(`Video ${status.jobId}: ${status.status} (${status.progress}%)`)\n      },\n    })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: 'A flying car over a city', duration: 5 })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Video'}\n      </button>\n\n      {isLoading && videoStatus && (\n        <div>\n          <p>Job: {jobId}</p>\n          <p>Status: {videoStatus.status}</p>\n          {videoStatus.progress != null && (\n            <progress value={videoStatus.progress} max={100} />\n          )}\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <video src={result.url} controls autoPlay style={{ maxWidth: '100%' }} />\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoGenerateInput"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text description of the desired video (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video size -- format depends on provider (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"16:9\""},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"1280x720\""},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video duration in seconds"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model-specific options"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateVideo"},{"type":"text","value":" returns two extra properties beyond the standard set:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"jobId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The current job ID, set when the server creates a video job"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"videoStatus"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoStatusInfo | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Live status updates with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"progress"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"jobId"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VideoStatusInfo"},{"type":"text","value":" type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface VideoStatusInfo {\n  jobId: string\n  status: 'pending' | 'processing' | 'completed' | 'failed'\n  progress?: number     // 0-100\n  url?: string          // Set when completed\n  error?: string        // Set when failed\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook also accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onJobCreated"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onStatusUpdate"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks for fine-grained tracking."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"base-hook-usegeneration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Base Hook: useGeneration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All specialized hooks are built on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGeneration"},{"type":"text","value":". Use it directly when you have a custom generation type that doesn't fit the built-in hooks."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGeneration, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\ninterface EmbeddingInput {\n  text: string\n  model?: string\n}\n\ninterface EmbeddingResult {\n  embedding: Array<number>\n  model: string\n  usage: { totalTokens: number }\n}\n\nfunction EmbeddingGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGeneration<\n    EmbeddingInput,\n    EmbeddingResult\n  >({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/embedding'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello world' })} disabled={isLoading}>\n        Generate Embedding\n      </button>\n      {result && <p>Dimensions: {result.embedding.length}</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseGenerationOptions<TInput, TResult>"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ConnectConnectionAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetcher"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationFetcher<TInput, TResult>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct async function (no streaming protocol needed)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ByokClient"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional keyring. Keys go in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" headers, never the body"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokProvider"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => ProviderId | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional provider slug. If it returns a slug, only that key is sent. Otherwise "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body.provider"},{"type":"text","value":". If no slug resolves, generate throws"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable scope for this generation. Required when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" is on. Optional for ephemeral runs."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional body parameters sent with connection requests"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(result: TResult) => TOutput | null | void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transform or react to results"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(error: Error) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error callback"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onProgress"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(progress: number, message?: string) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Progress updates (0-100)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(chunk: StreamChunk) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-chunk callback (connection mode only)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"return-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return Value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseGenerationReturn<TOutput>"},{"type":"text","value":" provides:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(input: TInput) => Promise<void>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trigger a generation request"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The generation result, or null"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether a generation is in progress"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current error, if any"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationClientState"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'idle'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'generating'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'success'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'error'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort the current generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear result, error, and return to idle"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"result-transforms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result Transforms"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"},{"type":"text","value":" callback can transform what gets stored in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { ImageGenerationResult } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst { result } = useGenerateImage({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n  onResult: (raw: ImageGenerationResult) => raw.images.map((img) => img.url || img.b64Json),\n})\n// result is now string[] instead of ImageGenerationResult","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"framework-variants","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework Variants"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All generation hooks are available across React, Vue, and Svelte with the same capabilities. The API shapes are identical -- only the naming convention and reactive primitives differ."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vue"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-svelte"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateImage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateImage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGenerateImage"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateAudio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateAudio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGenerateAudio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Speech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateSpeech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateSpeech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGenerateSpeech"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTranscription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useTranscription"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTranscription"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summarization"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSummarize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSummarize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSummarize"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateVideo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateVideo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGenerateVideo"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Base (generic)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGeneration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGeneration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGeneration"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three packages re-export "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchServerSentEvents"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":" for convenience."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Return values are wrapped in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DeepReadonly<ShallowRef<>>"},{"type":"text","value":" -- access them with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" in both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<template>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Functions use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*"},{"type":"text","value":" naming convention and return Svelte 5 reactive state via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$state"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./image-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Provider-specific options, sizes, and model availability"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Voice options, audio formats, and streaming audio"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./transcription","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcription"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- File formats, language detection, and word-level timestamps"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./video-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Job lifecycle, polling, and provider setup"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./generations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generations Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- Architecture and server-side streaming patterns"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"server-setup","text":"Server Setup","level":2},{"id":"usegenerateimage","text":"useGenerateImage","level":2},{"id":"usegenerateaudio","text":"useGenerateAudio","level":2},{"id":"usegeneratespeech","text":"useGenerateSpeech","level":2},{"id":"usetranscription","text":"useTranscription","level":2},{"id":"usesummarize","text":"useSummarize","level":2},{"id":"usegeneratevideo","text":"useGenerateVideo","level":2},{"id":"base-hook-usegeneration","text":"Base Hook: useGeneration","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"return-value","text":"Return Value","level":3},{"id":"result-transforms","text":"Result Transforms","level":3},{"id":"framework-variants","text":"Framework Variants","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack AI provides framework hooks for every generation type: image, audio, speech, transcription, summarization, and video. Each hook connects to a server endpoint and manages loading, error, and result state for you.\n\n> **Surviving reloads and dropped connections:** every generation hook takes the\n> same `persistence` option `useChat` does, so a long run's status and result\n> come back after a page reload or a dropped connection. It restores by\n> `threadId`, which for a generation names the slot successive runs fill\n> (`product-7-hero`) rather than a conversation. See\n> [Id map](../persistence/id-map). Setup is in\n> [Generation Persistence](../persistence/generation-persistence).\n\n## Overview\n\nGeneration hooks share a consistent API across all media types:\n\n| Hook | Input | Result Type |\n|------|-------|-------------|\n| `useGenerateImage` | `ImageGenerateInput` | `ImageGenerationResult` |\n| `useGenerateAudio` | `AudioGenerateInput` | `AudioGenerationResult` |\n| `useGenerateSpeech` | `SpeechGenerateInput` | `TTSResult` |\n| `useTranscription` | `TranscriptionGenerateInput` | `TranscriptionResult` |\n| `useSummarize` | `SummarizeGenerateInput` | `SummarizationResult` |\n| `useGenerateVideo` | `VideoGenerateInput` | `VideoGenerateResult` |\n| `useGeneration` | Generic `TInput` | Generic `TResult` |\n\nEvery hook returns the same core shape: `generate`, `result`, `isLoading`, `error`, `status`, `stop`, `reset`, and `runId` (the id of the job in flight, or `null`). You provide either a `connection` (streaming transport) or a `fetcher` (direct async call).\n\n## Server Setup\n\nBefore using hooks on the client, you need a server endpoint that runs the generation and returns the result as SSE. Here's a minimal image generation endpoint:\n\n```typescript\n// routes/api/generate/image.ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(req: Request) {\n  const { prompt, size, numberOfImages } = await req.json()\n\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: openaiImage('dall-e-3'),\n    prompt,\n    size,\n    numberOfImages,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThe same pattern applies to image, speech, transcription, summarize, and video. Live and world generation mint a session token. Connect in the browser. See [Live Generation](./live-generation) and [World Generation](./world-generation).\n\n## useGenerateImage\n\nTrigger image generation and render the results.\n\nFor a React + Start walkthrough with OpenRouter, open [Generate Image](../tutorials/generate-image).\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useState } from 'react'\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, reset } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(e) => setPrompt(e.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Describe an image...\"\n      />\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt })}\n        disabled={isLoading || !prompt.trim()}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img\n          key={i}\n          src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`}\n          alt={img.revisedPrompt || 'Generated image'}\n        />\n      ))}\n\n      {result && <button onClick={reset}>Clear</button>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts an `ImageGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `prompt` | `string` | Text description of the desired image (required) |\n| `numberOfImages` | `number` | Number of images to generate |\n| `size` | `string` | Image size in WIDTHxHEIGHT format (e.g., `\"1024x1024\"`) |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n## useGenerateAudio\n\nGenerate music or sound effects from a text prompt.\n\nWhen you use a `fetcher`, spread `options.headers` onto the POST. Pass `byok` so those headers include `x-byok-*` keys.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateAudio } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-client/byok'\n\nconst byok = defineByok({ storage: defaultByokStorage() })\n\nfunction AudioGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateAudio({\n    byok,\n    byokProvider: () => 'fal',\n    fetcher: async (input, options) => {\n      return fetch('/api/generate/audio', {\n        method: 'POST',\n        headers: {\n          'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n          ...options?.headers,\n        },\n        body: JSON.stringify(input),\n        signal: options?.signal,\n      })\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: 'An upbeat electronic track' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate'}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result?.audio.url && <audio src={result.audio.url} controls />}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nServer: read the header (or env), then run `generateAudio`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateAudio, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falAudio } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\nimport { falByok } from '@tanstack/ai-fal/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, falByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(falByok)\n\n  const body: unknown = await request.json()\n  if (typeof body !== 'object' || body === null || !('prompt' in body)) {\n    return new Response('Bad request', { status: 400 })\n  }\n  const prompt = body.prompt\n  if (typeof prompt !== 'string') {\n    return new Response('Bad request', { status: 400 })\n  }\n\n  const stream = generateAudio({\n    adapter: falAudio('fal-ai/minimax-music/v2.6', { apiKey }),\n    prompt,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts an `AudioGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `prompt` | `string` | Text description of the desired audio (required) |\n| `duration` | `number` | Desired duration in seconds |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\nSee [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for `defineByok` and a save UI.\n\n## useGenerateSpeech\n\nConvert text to speech and play it back.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useRef } from 'react'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const audioRef = useRef<HTMLAudioElement>(null)\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!', voice: 'alloy' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Speech'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <audio\n          ref={audioRef}\n          src={`data:audio/${result.format};base64,${result.audio}`}\n          controls\n          autoPlay\n        />\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `SpeechGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | `string` | The text to convert to speech (required) |\n| `voice` | `string` | The voice to use (e.g., `\"alloy\"`, `\"echo\"`) |\n| `format` | `'mp3' \\| 'opus' \\| 'aac' \\| 'flac' \\| 'wav' \\| 'pcm'` | Output audio format |\n| `speed` | `number` | Audio speed (0.25 to 4.0) |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\nThe `TTSResult` contains `audio` (base64-encoded), `format`, and optionally `duration` and `contentType`.\n\n## useTranscription\n\nTranscribe audio files to text.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useTranscription, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Transcriber() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useTranscription({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/transcribe'),\n  })\n\n  const handleFile = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n    const file = e.target.files?.[0]\n    if (file) {\n      const reader = new FileReader()\n      reader.onload = () => {\n        generate({ audio: reader.result as string, language: 'en' })\n      }\n      reader.readAsDataURL(file)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input type=\"file\" accept=\"audio/*\" onChange={handleFile} />\n\n      {isLoading && <p>Transcribing...</p>}\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <div>\n          <h3>Transcription</h3>\n          <p>{result.text}</p>\n          {result.language && <p>Language: {result.language}</p>}\n          {result.duration && <p>Duration: {result.duration}s</p>}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `TranscriptionGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `audio` | `string \\| File \\| Blob \\| ArrayBuffer` | Audio data -- base64 string, File, Blob, or ArrayBuffer (required) |\n| `language` | `string` | Language in ISO-639-1 format (e.g., `\"en\"`) |\n| `prompt` | `string` | Optional prompt to guide the transcription |\n| `responseFormat` | `'json' \\| 'text' \\| 'srt' \\| 'verbose_json' \\| 'vtt'` | Common output format |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n## useSummarize\n\nSummarize long text with configurable output styles.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useSummarize, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useState } from 'react'\n\nfunction Summarizer() {\n  const [text, setText] = useState('')\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useSummarize({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/summarize'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <textarea\n        value={text}\n        onChange={(e) => setText(e.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Paste text to summarize...\"\n        rows={8}\n      />\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text, style: 'bullet-points', maxLength: 200 })}\n        disabled={isLoading || !text.trim()}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Summarizing...' : 'Summarize'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <div>\n          <h3>Summary</h3>\n          <p>{result.summary}</p>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `SummarizeGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | `string` | The text to summarize (required) |\n| `maxLength` | `number` | Maximum length of the summary |\n| `style` | `'bullet-points' \\| 'paragraph' \\| 'concise'` | Summary style |\n| `focus` | `Array<string>` | Topics to focus on |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n## useGenerateVideo\n\nVideo generation is asynchronous -- a job is created on the server, then polled for status until completion. The hook manages the full lifecycle and exposes `jobId` and `videoStatus` so you can show progress.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateVideo, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction VideoGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, jobId, videoStatus, isLoading, error } =\n    useGenerateVideo({\n      connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/video'),\n      onStatusUpdate: (status) => {\n        console.log(`Video ${status.jobId}: ${status.status} (${status.progress}%)`)\n      },\n    })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: 'A flying car over a city', duration: 5 })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Video'}\n      </button>\n\n      {isLoading && videoStatus && (\n        <div>\n          <p>Job: {jobId}</p>\n          <p>Status: {videoStatus.status}</p>\n          {videoStatus.progress != null && (\n            <progress value={videoStatus.progress} max={100} />\n          )}\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <video src={result.url} controls autoPlay style={{ maxWidth: '100%' }} />\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `VideoGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `prompt` | `string` | Text description of the desired video (required) |\n| `size` | `string` | Video size -- format depends on provider (e.g., `\"16:9\"`, `\"1280x720\"`) |\n| `duration` | `number` | Video duration in seconds |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n`useGenerateVideo` returns two extra properties beyond the standard set:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `jobId` | `string \\| null` | The current job ID, set when the server creates a video job |\n| `videoStatus` | `VideoStatusInfo \\| null` | Live status updates with `status`, `progress`, and `jobId` |\n\nThe `VideoStatusInfo` type:\n\n```typescript\ninterface VideoStatusInfo {\n  jobId: string\n  status: 'pending' | 'processing' | 'completed' | 'failed'\n  progress?: number     // 0-100\n  url?: string          // Set when completed\n  error?: string        // Set when failed\n}\n```\n\nThe hook also accepts `onJobCreated` and `onStatusUpdate` callbacks for fine-grained tracking.\n\n## Base Hook: useGeneration\n\nAll specialized hooks are built on `useGeneration`. Use it directly when you have a custom generation type that doesn't fit the built-in hooks.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGeneration, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\ninterface EmbeddingInput {\n  text: string\n  model?: string\n}\n\ninterface EmbeddingResult {\n  embedding: Array<number>\n  model: string\n  usage: { totalTokens: number }\n}\n\nfunction EmbeddingGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGeneration<\n    EmbeddingInput,\n    EmbeddingResult\n  >({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/embedding'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello world' })} disabled={isLoading}>\n        Generate Embedding\n      </button>\n      {result && <p>Dimensions: {result.embedding.length}</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Options\n\n`UseGenerationOptions<TInput, TResult>` accepts:\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `connection` | `ConnectConnectionAdapter` | Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom) |\n| `fetcher` | `GenerationFetcher<TInput, TResult>` | Direct async function (no streaming protocol needed) |\n| `byok` | `ByokClient` | Optional keyring. Keys go in `x-byok-*` headers, never the body |\n| `byokProvider` | `() => ProviderId \\| undefined` | Optional provider slug. If it returns a slug, only that key is sent. Otherwise `body.provider`. If no slug resolves, generate throws |\n| `threadId` | `string` | Stable scope for this generation. Required when `persistence` is on. Optional for ephemeral runs. |\n| `body` | `Record<string, any>` | Additional body parameters sent with connection requests |\n| `onResult` | `(result: TResult) => TOutput \\| null \\| void` | Transform or react to results |\n| `onError` | `(error: Error) => void` | Error callback |\n| `onProgress` | `(progress: number, message?: string) => void` | Progress updates (0-100) |\n| `onChunk` | `(chunk: StreamChunk) => void` | Per-chunk callback (connection mode only) |\n\n### Return Value\n\n`UseGenerationReturn<TOutput>` provides:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `generate` | `(input: TInput) => Promise<void>` | Trigger a generation request |\n| `result` | `TOutput \\| null` | The generation result, or null |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean` | Whether a generation is in progress |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | Current error, if any |\n| `status` | `GenerationClientState` | `'idle'` \\| `'generating'` \\| `'success'` \\| `'error'` |\n| `stop` | `() => void` | Abort the current generation |\n| `reset` | `() => void` | Clear result, error, and return to idle |\n\n### Result Transforms\n\nThe `onResult` callback can transform what gets stored in `result`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { ImageGenerationResult } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst { result } = useGenerateImage({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n  onResult: (raw: ImageGenerationResult) => raw.images.map((img) => img.url || img.b64Json),\n})\n// result is now string[] instead of ImageGenerationResult\n```\n\n## Framework Variants\n\nAll generation hooks are available across React, Vue, and Svelte with the same capabilities. The API shapes are identical -- only the naming convention and reactive primitives differ.\n\n| Generation Type | React (`@tanstack/ai-react`) | Vue (`@tanstack/ai-vue`) | Svelte (`@tanstack/ai-svelte`) |\n|----------------|------------------------------|--------------------------|-------------------------------|\n| Image | `useGenerateImage` | `useGenerateImage` | `createGenerateImage` |\n| Audio | `useGenerateAudio` | `useGenerateAudio` | `createGenerateAudio` |\n| Speech | `useGenerateSpeech` | `useGenerateSpeech` | `createGenerateSpeech` |\n| Transcription | `useTranscription` | `useTranscription` | `createTranscription` |\n| Summarization | `useSummarize` | `useSummarize` | `createSummarize` |\n| Video | `useGenerateVideo` | `useGenerateVideo` | `createGenerateVideo` |\n| Base (generic) | `useGeneration` | `useGeneration` | `createGeneration` |\n\nAll three packages re-export `fetchServerSentEvents`, `fetchHttpStream`, and `stream` from `@tanstack/ai-client` for convenience.\n\n**Vue note:** Return values are wrapped in `DeepReadonly<ShallowRef<>>` -- access them with `.value` in both `<script>` and `<template>`.\n\n**Svelte note:** Functions use the `create*` naming convention and return Svelte 5 reactive state via `$state`.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Image Generation](./image-generation) -- Provider-specific options, sizes, and model availability\n- [Text-to-Speech](./text-to-speech) -- Voice options, audio formats, and streaming audio\n- [Transcription](./transcription) -- File formats, language detection, and word-level timestamps\n- [Video Generation](./video-generation) -- Job lifecycle, polling, and provider setup\n- [Generations Overview](./generations) -- Architecture and server-side streaming patterns\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Generation Hooks\nid: generation-hooks\norder: 7\ndescription: \"Framework hooks for every TanStack AI media generation type — useGenerateImage, useGenerateAudio, useGenerateSpeech, useTranscription, useSummarize, useGenerateVideo.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - generation hooks\n  - useGenerateImage\n  - useGenerateAudio\n  - useGenerateSpeech\n  - useTranscription\n  - useSummarize\n  - useGenerateVideo\n  - react hooks\n---\n\nTanStack AI provides framework hooks for every generation type: image, audio, speech, transcription, summarization, and video. Each hook connects to a server endpoint and manages loading, error, and result state for you.\n\n> **Surviving reloads and dropped connections:** every generation hook takes the\n> same `persistence` option `useChat` does, so a long run's status and result\n> come back after a page reload or a dropped connection. It restores by\n> `threadId`, which for a generation names the slot successive runs fill\n> (`product-7-hero`) rather than a conversation. See\n> [Id map](../persistence/id-map). Setup is in\n> [Generation Persistence](../persistence/generation-persistence).\n\n## Overview\n\nGeneration hooks share a consistent API across all media types:\n\n| Hook | Input | Result Type |\n|------|-------|-------------|\n| `useGenerateImage` | `ImageGenerateInput` | `ImageGenerationResult` |\n| `useGenerateAudio` | `AudioGenerateInput` | `AudioGenerationResult` |\n| `useGenerateSpeech` | `SpeechGenerateInput` | `TTSResult` |\n| `useTranscription` | `TranscriptionGenerateInput` | `TranscriptionResult` |\n| `useSummarize` | `SummarizeGenerateInput` | `SummarizationResult` |\n| `useGenerateVideo` | `VideoGenerateInput` | `VideoGenerateResult` |\n| `useGeneration` | Generic `TInput` | Generic `TResult` |\n\nEvery hook returns the same core shape: `generate`, `result`, `isLoading`, `error`, `status`, `stop`, `reset`, and `runId` (the id of the job in flight, or `null`). You provide either a `connection` (streaming transport) or a `fetcher` (direct async call).\n\n## Server Setup\n\nBefore using hooks on the client, you need a server endpoint that runs the generation and returns the result as SSE. Here's a minimal image generation endpoint:\n\n```typescript\n// routes/api/generate/image.ts\nimport { generateImage, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport async function POST(req: Request) {\n  const { prompt, size, numberOfImages } = await req.json()\n\n  const stream = generateImage({\n    adapter: openaiImage('dall-e-3'),\n    prompt,\n    size,\n    numberOfImages,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThe same pattern applies to image, speech, transcription, summarize, and video. Live and world generation mint a session token. Connect in the browser. See [Live Generation](./live-generation) and [World Generation](./world-generation).\n\n## useGenerateImage\n\nTrigger image generation and render the results.\n\nFor a React + Start walkthrough with OpenRouter, open [Generate Image](../tutorials/generate-image).\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useState } from 'react'\n\nfunction ImageGenerator() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('')\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error, reset } = useGenerateImage({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input\n        value={prompt}\n        onChange={(e) => setPrompt(e.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Describe an image...\"\n      />\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt })}\n        disabled={isLoading || !prompt.trim()}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result?.images.map((img, i) => (\n        <img\n          key={i}\n          src={img.url || `data:image/png;base64,${img.b64Json}`}\n          alt={img.revisedPrompt || 'Generated image'}\n        />\n      ))}\n\n      {result && <button onClick={reset}>Clear</button>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts an `ImageGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `prompt` | `string` | Text description of the desired image (required) |\n| `numberOfImages` | `number` | Number of images to generate |\n| `size` | `string` | Image size in WIDTHxHEIGHT format (e.g., `\"1024x1024\"`) |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n## useGenerateAudio\n\nGenerate music or sound effects from a text prompt.\n\nWhen you use a `fetcher`, spread `options.headers` onto the POST. Pass `byok` so those headers include `x-byok-*` keys.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateAudio } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-client/byok'\n\nconst byok = defineByok({ storage: defaultByokStorage() })\n\nfunction AudioGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateAudio({\n    byok,\n    byokProvider: () => 'fal',\n    fetcher: async (input, options) => {\n      return fetch('/api/generate/audio', {\n        method: 'POST',\n        headers: {\n          'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n          ...options?.headers,\n        },\n        body: JSON.stringify(input),\n        signal: options?.signal,\n      })\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: 'An upbeat electronic track' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate'}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result?.audio.url && <audio src={result.audio.url} controls />}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nServer: read the header (or env), then run `generateAudio`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateAudio, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falAudio } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\nimport { falByok } from '@tanstack/ai-fal/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, falByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(falByok)\n\n  const body: unknown = await request.json()\n  if (typeof body !== 'object' || body === null || !('prompt' in body)) {\n    return new Response('Bad request', { status: 400 })\n  }\n  const prompt = body.prompt\n  if (typeof prompt !== 'string') {\n    return new Response('Bad request', { status: 400 })\n  }\n\n  const stream = generateAudio({\n    adapter: falAudio('fal-ai/minimax-music/v2.6', { apiKey }),\n    prompt,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts an `AudioGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `prompt` | `string` | Text description of the desired audio (required) |\n| `duration` | `number` | Desired duration in seconds |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\nSee [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for `defineByok` and a save UI.\n\n## useGenerateSpeech\n\nConvert text to speech and play it back.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useRef } from 'react'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const audioRef = useRef<HTMLAudioElement>(null)\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!', voice: 'alloy' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Speech'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <audio\n          ref={audioRef}\n          src={`data:audio/${result.format};base64,${result.audio}`}\n          controls\n          autoPlay\n        />\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `SpeechGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | `string` | The text to convert to speech (required) |\n| `voice` | `string` | The voice to use (e.g., `\"alloy\"`, `\"echo\"`) |\n| `format` | `'mp3' \\| 'opus' \\| 'aac' \\| 'flac' \\| 'wav' \\| 'pcm'` | Output audio format |\n| `speed` | `number` | Audio speed (0.25 to 4.0) |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\nThe `TTSResult` contains `audio` (base64-encoded), `format`, and optionally `duration` and `contentType`.\n\n## useTranscription\n\nTranscribe audio files to text.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useTranscription, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Transcriber() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useTranscription({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/transcribe'),\n  })\n\n  const handleFile = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n    const file = e.target.files?.[0]\n    if (file) {\n      const reader = new FileReader()\n      reader.onload = () => {\n        generate({ audio: reader.result as string, language: 'en' })\n      }\n      reader.readAsDataURL(file)\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input type=\"file\" accept=\"audio/*\" onChange={handleFile} />\n\n      {isLoading && <p>Transcribing...</p>}\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <div>\n          <h3>Transcription</h3>\n          <p>{result.text}</p>\n          {result.language && <p>Language: {result.language}</p>}\n          {result.duration && <p>Duration: {result.duration}s</p>}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `TranscriptionGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `audio` | `string \\| File \\| Blob \\| ArrayBuffer` | Audio data -- base64 string, File, Blob, or ArrayBuffer (required) |\n| `language` | `string` | Language in ISO-639-1 format (e.g., `\"en\"`) |\n| `prompt` | `string` | Optional prompt to guide the transcription |\n| `responseFormat` | `'json' \\| 'text' \\| 'srt' \\| 'verbose_json' \\| 'vtt'` | Common output format |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n## useSummarize\n\nSummarize long text with configurable output styles.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useSummarize, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { useState } from 'react'\n\nfunction Summarizer() {\n  const [text, setText] = useState('')\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useSummarize({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/summarize'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <textarea\n        value={text}\n        onChange={(e) => setText(e.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Paste text to summarize...\"\n        rows={8}\n      />\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text, style: 'bullet-points', maxLength: 200 })}\n        disabled={isLoading || !text.trim()}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Summarizing...' : 'Summarize'}\n      </button>\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <div>\n          <h3>Summary</h3>\n          <p>{result.summary}</p>\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `SummarizeGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | `string` | The text to summarize (required) |\n| `maxLength` | `number` | Maximum length of the summary |\n| `style` | `'bullet-points' \\| 'paragraph' \\| 'concise'` | Summary style |\n| `focus` | `Array<string>` | Topics to focus on |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n## useGenerateVideo\n\nVideo generation is asynchronous -- a job is created on the server, then polled for status until completion. The hook manages the full lifecycle and exposes `jobId` and `videoStatus` so you can show progress.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateVideo, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction VideoGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, jobId, videoStatus, isLoading, error } =\n    useGenerateVideo({\n      connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/video'),\n      onStatusUpdate: (status) => {\n        console.log(`Video ${status.jobId}: ${status.status} (${status.progress}%)`)\n      },\n    })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ prompt: 'A flying car over a city', duration: 5 })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Video'}\n      </button>\n\n      {isLoading && videoStatus && (\n        <div>\n          <p>Job: {jobId}</p>\n          <p>Status: {videoStatus.status}</p>\n          {videoStatus.progress != null && (\n            <progress value={videoStatus.progress} max={100} />\n          )}\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n\n      {result && (\n        <video src={result.url} controls autoPlay style={{ maxWidth: '100%' }} />\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe `generate` function accepts a `VideoGenerateInput`:\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `prompt` | `string` | Text description of the desired video (required) |\n| `size` | `string` | Video size -- format depends on provider (e.g., `\"16:9\"`, `\"1280x720\"`) |\n| `duration` | `number` | Video duration in seconds |\n| `modelOptions` | `Record<string, any>` | Model-specific options |\n\n`useGenerateVideo` returns two extra properties beyond the standard set:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `jobId` | `string \\| null` | The current job ID, set when the server creates a video job |\n| `videoStatus` | `VideoStatusInfo \\| null` | Live status updates with `status`, `progress`, and `jobId` |\n\nThe `VideoStatusInfo` type:\n\n```typescript\ninterface VideoStatusInfo {\n  jobId: string\n  status: 'pending' | 'processing' | 'completed' | 'failed'\n  progress?: number     // 0-100\n  url?: string          // Set when completed\n  error?: string        // Set when failed\n}\n```\n\nThe hook also accepts `onJobCreated` and `onStatusUpdate` callbacks for fine-grained tracking.\n\n## Base Hook: useGeneration\n\nAll specialized hooks are built on `useGeneration`. Use it directly when you have a custom generation type that doesn't fit the built-in hooks.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGeneration, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\ninterface EmbeddingInput {\n  text: string\n  model?: string\n}\n\ninterface EmbeddingResult {\n  embedding: Array<number>\n  model: string\n  usage: { totalTokens: number }\n}\n\nfunction EmbeddingGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGeneration<\n    EmbeddingInput,\n    EmbeddingResult\n  >({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/embedding'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello world' })} disabled={isLoading}>\n        Generate Embedding\n      </button>\n      {result && <p>Dimensions: {result.embedding.length}</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Options\n\n`UseGenerationOptions<TInput, TResult>` accepts:\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `connection` | `ConnectConnectionAdapter` | Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom) |\n| `fetcher` | `GenerationFetcher<TInput, TResult>` | Direct async function (no streaming protocol needed) |\n| `byok` | `ByokClient` | Optional keyring. Keys go in `x-byok-*` headers, never the body |\n| `byokProvider` | `() => ProviderId \\| undefined` | Optional provider slug. If it returns a slug, only that key is sent. Otherwise `body.provider`. If no slug resolves, generate throws |\n| `threadId` | `string` | Stable scope for this generation. Required when `persistence` is on. Optional for ephemeral runs. |\n| `body` | `Record<string, any>` | Additional body parameters sent with connection requests |\n| `onResult` | `(result: TResult) => TOutput \\| null \\| void` | Transform or react to results |\n| `onError` | `(error: Error) => void` | Error callback |\n| `onProgress` | `(progress: number, message?: string) => void` | Progress updates (0-100) |\n| `onChunk` | `(chunk: StreamChunk) => void` | Per-chunk callback (connection mode only) |\n\n### Return Value\n\n`UseGenerationReturn<TOutput>` provides:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `generate` | `(input: TInput) => Promise<void>` | Trigger a generation request |\n| `result` | `TOutput \\| null` | The generation result, or null |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean` | Whether a generation is in progress |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | Current error, if any |\n| `status` | `GenerationClientState` | `'idle'` \\| `'generating'` \\| `'success'` \\| `'error'` |\n| `stop` | `() => void` | Abort the current generation |\n| `reset` | `() => void` | Clear result, error, and return to idle |\n\n### Result Transforms\n\nThe `onResult` callback can transform what gets stored in `result`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateImage, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { ImageGenerationResult } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst { result } = useGenerateImage({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/image'),\n  onResult: (raw: ImageGenerationResult) => raw.images.map((img) => img.url || img.b64Json),\n})\n// result is now string[] instead of ImageGenerationResult\n```\n\n## Framework Variants\n\nAll generation hooks are available across React, Vue, and Svelte with the same capabilities. The API shapes are identical -- only the naming convention and reactive primitives differ.\n\n| Generation Type | React (`@tanstack/ai-react`) | Vue (`@tanstack/ai-vue`) | Svelte (`@tanstack/ai-svelte`) |\n|----------------|------------------------------|--------------------------|-------------------------------|\n| Image | `useGenerateImage` | `useGenerateImage` | `createGenerateImage` |\n| Audio | `useGenerateAudio` | `useGenerateAudio` | `createGenerateAudio` |\n| Speech | `useGenerateSpeech` | `useGenerateSpeech` | `createGenerateSpeech` |\n| Transcription | `useTranscription` | `useTranscription` | `createTranscription` |\n| Summarization | `useSummarize` | `useSummarize` | `createSummarize` |\n| Video | `useGenerateVideo` | `useGenerateVideo` | `createGenerateVideo` |\n| Base (generic) | `useGeneration` | `useGeneration` | `createGeneration` |\n\nAll three packages re-export `fetchServerSentEvents`, `fetchHttpStream`, and `stream` from `@tanstack/ai-client` for convenience.\n\n**Vue note:** Return values are wrapped in `DeepReadonly<ShallowRef<>>` -- access them with `.value` in both `<script>` and `<template>`.\n\n**Svelte note:** Functions use the `create*` naming convention and return Svelte 5 reactive state via `$state`.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Image Generation](./image-generation) -- Provider-specific options, sizes, and model availability\n- [Text-to-Speech](./text-to-speech) -- Voice options, audio formats, and streaming audio\n- [Transcription](./transcription) -- File formats, language detection, and word-level timestamps\n- [Video Generation](./video-generation) -- Job lifecycle, polling, and provider setup\n- [Generations Overview](./generations) -- Architecture and server-side streaming patterns\n"}
